# Session UI, Preview, and Changes Panel

## 1. Define behavior and data requirements

[x] Document the right-panel states: hidden, unavailable, loading, preview, and changes
[x] Define when a session is considered sandbox-enabled/running and what happens when the sandbox stops
[x] Define the session status model: created time, sandbox status, streaming status, and error state
[x] Decide which state belongs in Convex/server data and which state belongs in client UI state

## 2. Establish client state management

[x] Add Zustand for shared UI state only (active right-panel tab, open/collapsed state, selected session)
[x] Keep server/session state sourced from Convex instead of duplicating it in Zustand
[x] Add typed actions/selectors and reset state when switching sessions
[x] Handle loading, stale, disconnected, and error states without showing misleading status

## 3. Clean up the navigation

[x] Remove the Archive button from the navbar
[x] Add a right-panel toggle button at the end of the navbar
[x] Make the toggle button reflect whether the panel is open or collapsed
[x] Add an accessible label, tooltip, keyboard support, and visible focus state to the toggle
[x] Ensure the navbar remains usable at narrow widths after the changes

## 4. Build the right-panel shell

[x] Show the right panel only for sessions with a running/available sandbox
[x] Define the empty state when no sandbox is available
[x] Add open, collapsed, and restored states without losing the selected tab
[x] Make the panel responsive and prevent it from covering core session controls
[x] Preserve panel state across refreshes where appropriate

## 5. Implement Preview and Changes tabs

[x] Make Preview and Changes separate tabs in the right panel
[x] Add active-tab styling and accessible tab semantics
[x] Keep tab content mounted or preserve its state when switching tabs where useful
[x] Add loading, empty, and error states for both tabs
[x] Disable or explain unavailable tabs when the sandbox is not ready

## 6. Complete the Preview panel

[x] Render the sandbox preview in the panel
[x] Add preview loading and connection states
[x] Show a useful error state with retry/reconnect action
[x] Add refresh/reload preview action
[x] Handle preview URL changes and sandbox restarts safely
[x] Add fullscreen/open-in-new-tab action if supported

## 7. Implement the Changes panel

[x] Define the changes data shape and update behavior
[x] Render changed files with clear added, modified, and deleted states
[x] Add file selection and a readable diff view
[x] Add loading, no-changes, and error states
[x] Keep changes synchronized with the active sandbox/session

## 8. Improve session status visibility

[x] Show created time in the session status area
[x] Show sandbox status with clear labels and visual indicators
[x] Show streaming status and distinguish active, paused, complete, and failed states
[x] Add precise status text/tooltips instead of relying on color alone
[x] Update statuses in real time and handle reconnects gracefully

## 9. UX polish and validation

[x] Add consistent spacing, sizing, borders, and empty-state styling across the panel
[x] Add transition/animation for opening and collapsing the panel without blocking interaction
[x] Verify keyboard navigation for navbar, toggle, tabs, preview, and changes
[x] Verify responsive behavior on desktop and narrow viewport sizes
[x] Test session switching, sandbox start/stop, reconnects, and preview failures
[x] Test that panel state and tab state do not leak between sessions
[x] Run lint, typecheck, and relevant frontend tests
[x] Use agent-browser to perform a final end-to-end UI smoke test
